  "end_via_stacks_ohm": 27.6,
  "conclusion": "R3 finding: column write-line IR-drop is NEGLIGIBLE for small columns (N<=64 on metal: <5% of the 776 ohm device) but becomes SIGNIFICANT for tall columns (N=256 -> ~16% on met1/met2 W=1um; ~6% on met3), and is CATASTROPHIC on li1 (kohm). Design guidance: route the write line on met2+ (never li1/poly), widen it, or segment tall columns; budget ~10-20% write headroom/energy for N>=256. This refines errata R3 (IR-drop) and adds the R_par/776 series overhead to the R5 end-to-end write energy (E_dev=0.783 pJ -> +16.5% at N=256 met2)."
